{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms","id":1112444,"title":"Thinking about \"off-Aspect\" Dragon-Blooded Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-06T18:29:41-07:00","id":1112444,"title":"Thinking about \"off-Aspect\" Dragon-Blooded Charms","content":"It must be such a great time to be a Dragon-Blooded fan, because I'm becoming more of one each day I think about what they're going to be like in Third Edition. Specialized Excellencies, Signature Charms, the Aura State system, and Charms of every elemental Aspect in each of the 25 Abilities.<br /> <br /> That last item is what I want to talk about, here. I want to share some ideas I have for Charm concepts we might see, and that I would like to see.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see your ideas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ARCHERY (Wood)</b><br /> <br /> The original Wood Aspect Charmset for Archery Charms was cool, and I'm hoping to see tricks like Harvest of the Hunter expanding into the promised trick of creating an entire Womping Willow tree from your bow.<br /> <br /> Air-aspect Charms can control air currents to provide additional range, cut through inclement weather, and defeat cover. Hunter's Unobstructed Aim is going to become even less obstructed. There's also the ideas of shooting lightning bolts as arrows, or shooting clouds to produce rain and lightning.<br /> <br /> Earth-aspect Charms might work upon metal arrowheads as Wood-magic works upon shafts. Otherwise, I could see dragon-arrows creating sinkholes and earthquakes as they strike the earth like meteorites.<br /> <br /> Fire-magic means that Solar Exalted aren't the only ones shooting flaming, exploding arrows around. But here's hoping that we see some honest-to-goodness FIREWAND Charms. Maybe they'll have grafted in the Terrestrial Charms from Golden Exhalation Style?<br /> <br /> I'm not too clear on Water tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>ATHLETICS (Fire)</b><br /> <br /> Effortlessly Rising Flame might become a Dodge Charm, now that rising from prone is rolled with Dodge when rolled at all. It would be right at home with Hopping Firecracker Evasion.<br /> <br /> Fire-magic has always provided the &quot;blazing speed&quot; that Dragon-Blooded Athletics needs, but now Air-magic can provide the aerial grace that it has previously lacked. They may have even better floating tricks than Solars.<br /> <br /> Earth-magic will finally let Dragon-Blooded stand upside-down on ceilings. Perfect Climbing Attitude could have found a new home in this Ability if not for the fact that climbing is sort of pointless next to running or flying up walls.<br /> <br /> Water-magic will, of course, finally make Fire Aspects great swimmers.<br /> <br /> Wood-magic, Vance has said, will contribute the vital lifting power of a tree that steadily raises up the great weight of its growing branches and fruit. It might also include the creeping, tearing strength of roots that break apart soil and stone.<br /> <br /> Earth and Wood magic together will likely allow Dragon-Blooded to lift great masses of stone, wood, or living creatures, and hurl them great distances -- possibly with the aid of Air for more distance.<br /> <br /> Earth might further contribute power for breaking apart stone targets, or bearing up great weights for long periods of time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>AWARENESS (Earth)</b><br /> <br /> Air-magic for hearing sounds on the wind, and catching scents on the breeze.<br /> <br /> Fire-magic for seeing in the dark with the smallest amount of light, producing enough light to illuminate or even blind, and also protection against being blinded. Sense-Destroying Method and Essence Disruption Attack also fit the violent Essence of Fire.<br /> <br /> Wood-magic might help the Dragon-Blooded become more aware of the particular scents of specific people, beasts, and plants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CRAFT (Earth)</b><br /> <br /> Air-magic might include Charms that greatly assist the repair and construction of Artifacts, owing to how Occult and Lore are Air-aspected Abilities vital to those actions. In a Modernized Creation, this would also seem like a good Aspect for fixing and making electronic devices, which also resonates with how computer science is based on Lore.<br /> <br /> Fire, of course, is natural for assisting in metalworking, ceramics, and glassblowing, as well as any object-destruction Charms you might find in Dragon-Blooded Craft. Fire has a habit of finding and consuming any flaw.<br /> <br /> Water might finally give us Charms specifically for cooking food, as well as preparing medicines, poisons, perfumes, and make-up.<br /> <br /> Wood would be carpentry, obviously. Possibly even the power to shape living trees into the forms the Prince of the Earth desires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>DODGE (Fire)</b><br /> <br /> Again, Air provides some of the grace that Fire lacked.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I don't have much. But I kind of hope we see the elemental-based Clone Jutsus seen in <i>Naruto</i> -- Mud Clones, Sand Clones, Water Clones, Smoke Clones, or simple substitution logs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 07-06-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T18:56:35-07:00","id":1112450,"title":"","content":"<b>INTEGRITY (Earth)</b><br /> <br /> Air-magic is perfect for meditation Charms, as well as refuting social influence with rational, fact-based logic, and perhaps also protecting Principles that take the form of high-minded ideals.<br /> <br /> Fire-magic might be better for refuting social influence with passionate feelings, and protecting Ties.<br /> <br /> Water-magic is natural for refuting social influence through slippery logic, legal-ese, twisting the letter of an agreement, and finding tortured justifications.<br /> <br /> Wood-magic offers the perfect metaphor for treating your values like a garden -- pruning unwanted Intimacies while nursing passions and grudges into lusty flowers or weeds. Combined with Earth and Air's meditation, it can also help restore the body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INVESTIGATION (Water)</b><br /> <br /> Not really sure about this one, beyond Fire's ability to illuminate the dark of the underworld and threaten anyone whom an investigator needs to confess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LINGUISTICS (Air)</b><br /> <br /> I don't know. Fire might give you the power to scorch words into surfaces with a burning fingertip, or write messages of shining fire in the empty air?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>LORE (Air)</b><br /> <br /> Earth-magic could help a Dragon-Blooded Lore specialist understand the purpose and function of First Age artifacts. In a Modernized Creation, it could also lend itself to writing computer code.<br /> <br /> Water-magic would excel at computer hacking.<br /> <br /> Fire-magic might help with illuminating minds and inspiring a passion to learn.<br /> <br /> Wood-magic might also lend metaphors of planting seeds in the minds of others.<br /> <br /> The Elemental Bolt/Burst Charms might become more varied.<br /> <br /> I think either Lore or Integrity might contain Charms to provide new ways to use or control the Aura State mechanic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>MEDICINE (Wood)</b><br /> <br /> Air... I'm not sure. Perhaps dealing with mental disorders, a la Madness-Analyzing Stare?<br /> <br /> Earth might offer ways to surgically remove foreign objects, as well as surgically graft on replacement prosthetic limbs. It could also include massage, chiropractic adjustment, and possibly acupuncture.<br /> <br /> Fire would treat diseases through fevers, as well as working to sterilize and cauterize in general. There's also moxibustion and heat-treatment therapies, like those seen from Jackie Chan's character in the remake of <i>Karate Kid</i>.<br /> <br /> Water... treating patients with medicine and food?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:53:53-07:00","id":1112507,"title":"","content":"It's late for me, but marking this thread to comment tomorrow hopefully. I enjoy elemental discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T22:15:16-07:00","id":1112509,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it would work better for Medicine or Intimacy, but I had the thought of treating mental illness and other distress in a magical garden; there's a linguistic evidence I can't recall right now, something to do with paradise or possibly gardens.<br /> Other preliminary thoughts: I imagine Earth Craft to be useful for large-scale projects, like raising buildings and infrastructure. Water Archery provides arrows that can slip through cracks in armor and dissolve after impact (ironically 'soak' would be less useful in this case). Air Investigation I imagine to help with mind-palace style analysis. I really like your thoughts on Fire Lore. Air Medicine might involve breathing techniques and other methods of realigning Essence, which I imagine might help to fight supernatural afflictions like curses and magical effects. Don't know if that's a little beyond the purview of Medicine, but maybe they can branch out a little at higher Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T08:47:18-07:00","id":1112707,"title":"","content":"Dodge was the first to catch my attention.<br /> <br /> Fire: Flash bang to lower attack before it hits you, smoke bomb to increase your dodge<br /> Earth: Short range teleport by sinking into the earth and rising out a range band away<br /> Air: Path of frost to slide across to disengage, turning into air so a weapon passes through you<br /> Water: Similar to above turn to water and weapon passes through you<br /> Wood: This is the one I get the most stuck on, because everything I think of is parry. Maybe increase dodge from wood weapons? Seems weak<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T09:21:47-07:00","id":1112729,"title":"","content":"BUREAUCRACY (Water)<br /> <br /> Air magic for clear communication and distant coordination.<br /> <br /> Earth Bureaucracy for straightening out an organization.<br /> <br /> Fire Bureaucracy for destroying an organization.<br /> <br /> Wood Bureaucracy for growing an organization.<br /> <br /> Earth/Wood Bureaucracy for tracking/marking fiat currency.<br /> <br /> <br /> LARCENY (Water)<br /> <br /> Air Larceny for quick and quiet pickpocketing and card-switching<br /> <br /> Earth Larceny for hiding things in stone and making counterfeits?<br /> <br /> <br /> MELEE (Fire)<br /> <br /> Air Melee for throwing and retrieving weapons.<br /> <br /> Earth Melee for stone and metal weapons, maybe smashing weapons.<br /> <br /> Water Melee for defeating armor; Piercing weapons?<br /> <br /> Wood Melee for poisons and wooden weapons; Chopping weapons, as like tree-felling axes? Flexibile and grappling weapons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:25:41-07:00","id":1112778,"title":"","content":"Water Awareness for reacting to surprises and other rapidly changing situations.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Water War; changing strategies in response to new situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:36:15-07:00","id":1112785,"title":"","content":"PERFORMANCE (Wood)<br /> <br /> Air Performance for wind instruments and dancing, possibly oratory. Voice projection and throwing.<br /> <br /> Earth Performance for percussive instruments and playing the earth itself like a drum. Dancing hard enough to shake the earth?<br /> <br /> Fire Performance for sex, dancing, rock and roll, fiery oratory.<br /> <br /> Water Performance for dancing, acting, and disguising your voice.<br /> <br /> <br /> PRESENCE (Fire)<br /> <br /> Air Presence arguing for Principles<br /> <br /> Earth Presence arguing for Principles<br /> <br /> Water Presence for lies and manipulation<br /> <br /> Wood Presence for seduction<br /> <br /> <br /> OCCULT (Air)<br /> <br /> Earth Occult for creating enduring sorcerous works, understanding geomancy, working with earth elementals, forcing spirits to manifest<br /> <br /> Fire Occult for destroying spirits, casting destructive sorcery, distorting spells, fire elementals<br /> <br /> Water Occult for water elementals<br /> <br /> Wood Occult for wood elementals and creating life with sorcerous works<br /> <br /> <br /> RESISTANCE (Earth)<br /> <br /> Air Resistance for not running out of breath<br /> <br /> Fire Resistance for absorbing energy attacks and entering a battle-rage<br /> <br /> Water Resistance for resisting poison and donning armor<br /> <br /> Wood Resistance for resisting disease, recovering from injury, and forming wooden armor","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:23:11-07:00","id":1112918,"title":"","content":"Earth Awareness: Straight up Toph. Reading your opponent through the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:22:47-07:00","id":1112954,"title":"","content":"Fire War: Attack, attack, attack. If particularly gritty, morale damage and use of fire for civilian destruction and intimidation<br /> Air War: Rapid strikes and withdrawls. Some ranged fighting. <br /> Wood War: Ranged/Archer boosts. Cover use, gurriella fighting, surviving off the land easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:50:35-07:00","id":1112992,"title":"","content":"Water Archery: An arrow that flows effortlessly around obstacles, or an arrow fired into the air that comes down later as a literal rain of arrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13529-canisinvictus","name":"CanisInvictus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T00:49:57-07:00","id":1115421,"title":"","content":"Here's some that occurred to me, all for Brawl.<br /> <br /> Air Brawl: Be swift. Be rapid. Never place all your power into one blow. Instead, strike fast and often enough for your foe to have no chance of blocking your attack.<br /> Earth Brawl: Be firm. Be resolute. When you strike your foe, strike as a landslide or avalanche. One can see those approach, but they are unable to evade such might.<br /> Fire Brawl: Start soft, but grow. As a flame grows brighter as it consumes more, build your strikes until you are an unstoppable force your foe cannot face.<br /> Wood Brawl: Given time, even a humble plant root can grow into the cracks in all things, and split them apart. Be as the wood: Find the flaws in your opponent and exploit them. NO defense can stand against a strike in the exact right location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:07:11-07:00","id":1115494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115421#post1115421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's some that occurred to me, all for Brawl.<br /> <br /> Air Brawl: Be swift. Be rapid. Never place all your power into one blow. Instead, strike fast and often enough for your foe to have no chance of blocking your attack.<br /> Earth Brawl: Be firm. Be resolute. When you strike your foe, strike as a landslide or avalanche. One can see those approach, but they are unable to evade such might.<br /> Fire Brawl: Start soft, but grow. As a flame grows brighter as it consumes more, build your strikes until you are an unstoppable force your foe cannot face.<br /> Wood Brawl: Given time, even a humble plant root can grow into the cracks in all things, and split them apart. Be as the wood: Find the flaws in your opponent and exploit them. NO defense can stand against a strike in the exact right location.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Vance if Terrestrial attack Ability Charmtrees would share the same strategies as the Solar ones... such as Brawl having awful defense but a powerful capacity for building a lot of Initiative quickly.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Melee would feature slow gains from behind solid defense. If those gains are slow enough, then a &quot;building power&quot; theme would be appropriate in Terrestrial Brawl. But if Brawl's gains are too fast and instant, the &quot;building power&quot; theme might work better in Melee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T07:25:32-07:00","id":1115515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115421#post1115421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's some that occurred to me, all for Brawl.<br /> <br /> Air Brawl: Be swift. Be rapid. Never place all your power into one blow. Instead, strike fast and often enough for your foe to have no chance of blocking your attack.<br /> Earth Brawl: Be firm. Be resolute. When you strike your foe, strike as a landslide or avalanche. One can see those approach, but they are unable to evade such might.<br /> Fire Brawl: Start soft, but grow. As a flame grows brighter as it consumes more, build your strikes until you are an unstoppable force your foe cannot face.<br /> Wood Brawl: Given time, even a humble plant root can grow into the cracks in all things, and split them apart. Be as the wood: Find the flaws in your opponent and exploit them. NO defense can stand against a strike in the exact right location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! What about Water Brawl, any ideas? I'm thinking, be fluid, soak all damage just like water can't really be hurt, roll with the blow, in the same vein, and strike once, but with all the frightening force of a tsunami. Sheesh, I'm becoming a DB fan too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:56:24-07:00","id":1115598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115515#post1115515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! What about Water Brawl, any ideas? I'm thinking, be fluid, soak all damage just like water can't really be hurt, roll with the blow, in the same vein, and strike once, but with all the frightening force of a tsunami. Sheesh, I'm becoming a DB fan too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mention water Brawl because this is the OUT of Aspect thread, and Brawl is, AFAIK, a Water-primary Ability. On 2E, the innate Terrestrial Hero Style (which will likely be the core DB Brawl charms of Ex3) was very much &quot;Be water. Flow, strike, and batter your foe like crashing waves&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:25:48-07:00","id":1115628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115598#post1115598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mention water Brawl because this is the OUT of Aspect thread, and Brawl is, AFAIK, a Water-primary Ability. On 2E, the innate Terrestrial Hero Style (which will likely be the core DB Brawl charms of Ex3) was very much &amp;quot;Be water. Flow, strike, and batter your foe like crashing waves&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, freezing them in ice when you're not literally drowning them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:28:53-07:00","id":1115630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115598#post1115598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mention water Brawl because this is the OUT of Aspect thread, and Brawl is, AFAIK, a Water-primary Ability. On 2E, the innate Terrestrial Hero Style (which will likely be the core DB Brawl charms of Ex3) was very much &quot;Be water. Flow, strike, and batter your foe like crashing waves&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, didn't know. Looked at the Ex2 Aspect abilities and didn't see Brawl... must've missed it. Whoops, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T12:41:35-07:00","id":1115638,"title":"","content":"It was called Martial Arts in 2nd ed.<br /> Well, actually Water Aspects still have Martial Arts, they just have Brawl as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:13:19-07:00","id":1115718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1112444-thinking-about-off-aspect-dragon-blooded-charms?p=1115630#post1115630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, didn't know. Looked at the Ex2 Aspect abilities and didn't see Brawl... must've missed it. Whoops, sorry!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what Oz said. Brawl was removed in Ex2 to give Martial Arts as an innate ability. Instead, each Splat had a selection of native Martial Arts Charms, the center tree of which could be learned by any other splat as a Hero Style. So you had Solar Hero Style, Lunar Hero Style, Terrestrial Hero Style, etc.<br /> <br /> Ex3 gently tossed that out and now innate unarmed combat styles are just Brawl, which was an ability in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:39:23-07:00","id":1116865,"title":"","content":"I think it would be cool if Melee included Charms for fighting with wooden weapons. Especially if you could soak poison into those weapons, as per Second Edition's Ill Lily Style.<br /> <br /> Melee Charms could let a Dragon-Blood produce wooden weapons from her Essence, as well as produce the poison.<br /> <br /> Or produce strong vines for use as whips and lassos.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Brawl could introduce grappling Charms that let you bind your clinched opponent in ice (Water+Air), vines or thorny vines, or even beckon the earth itself to rise up and hold them.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Melee or Brawl might include an Earth Charm that lets you strike a prone character to embed them firmly into the ground, making it harder for them to get back on their feet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Thrown could support the cold of Air with the moisture of Water to freeze opponents in place at a distance, or perhaps to alter the protection of Whirlwind Shield Form into Mei's Ice Wall ability.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded Thrown could include Wood Charms for binding opponents with bolas, nets, and lassos. Thorny, poisonous bolas, nets, and lassos.<br /> <br /> Stony javelins that explode to shred targets with shrapnel?<br /> <br /> Air + Earth for blinding, choking sand blasts?<br /> <br /> Air + Fire for lightning blasts?<br /> <br /> Could Dragon-Blooded refine their Wind Weapons enough to achieve aerokinetic telekinesis? For fine manipulation from a distance? That would be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}